DSFILTER(1)                    ZOAU Command Syntax                   DSFILTER(1)

NAME

	dsfilter - Filter output from LISTCAT command (via stdin)

SYNOPSIS

	dsfilter [-dhv]

	-d
		Print debug information.

	-h
		Print syntax information.

	-v
		Print verbose information.


DESCRIPTION

	This command is intended as a 'helper' script for other commands.

	dsfilter takes raw output from the LISTCAT command output and writes
	out information in the form:
		<type> <name> <volume>
	where <type> indicates the type of dataset being listed, and volume
	is the volume the dataset resides on (if the dataset is on multiple
	volumes, the volume displayed will be the first volume).
	If the dataset is migrated, the volume will show as MIGRAT.

	<type> may be:
		CATALOG:   the dataset is a catalog
		PAGESPACE: the dataset is a pagespace
		NONVSAM:   the dataset is sequential or partitioned
		CLUSTER:   the dataset is a VSAM cluster
		DATA:      the dataset is a VSAM DATA dataset
		INDEX:     the dataset is a VSAM INDEX dataset
		ALIAS:     the dataset is an alias of another dataset
		GDGBASER:  the dataset is a GDG base dataset
		AIX:       the dataset is an AIX dataset

EXAMPLES

	See dlsraw for usage.

EXIT VALUES

	0
		Processing completed normally

	other
		Error occurred. See error messages for details.

SEE ALSO

	dlsraw(1)
